  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Service-Disabled Veteran-Owned Small Business (SDVOSB) set-aside contracting reached $9.6B in FY2026 to date. The federal government made 15,273 awards under SDVOSB set-asides, with an average award size of $627K. Obligations increased year over year, up 10.1% from the prior fiscal period. Fiscal history shows a multi-year climb from $7.2B in FY21 to $9.6B in FY26, with interim totals of $8B in FY22, $9.1B in FY23, $8.8B in FY24, and $8.7B in FY25. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction and Other Computer Related Services are the two largest industry recipients, together accounting for a substantial share of FY2026 to date obligations. The Department of Veterans Affairs accounted for the largest agency share at $7.8B. The top vendor was V3GATE, LLC at $577M, followed by FOUR POINTS TECHNOLOGY, L.L.C. at $277M and SPREZZATURA MANAGEMENT CONSULTING, LLC at $241M. This dataset covers contract obligations and represents fiscal year to date totals that are partial for the current year.",
    "sections": [
      {
        "heading": "What is the overall size and recent trend in SDVOSB set-aside obligations?",
        "body": "The federal government obligated $9.6B to SDVOSB set-asides in FY2026 to date. Obligations rose year over year, up 10.1%. The program delivered 15,273 awards at an average award size of $627K. Fiscal year comparisons show growth from $7.2B in FY21 to $9.6B in FY26."
      },
      {
        "heading": "Where is SDVOSB spending concentrated by agency and industry?",
        "body": "The Department of Veterans Affairs obligated $7.8B in FY2026 to date, the largest agency share. Department of Defense obligations totaled $856M, followed by Department of Homeland Security at $214M and Department of Transportation at $133M. Commercial and Institutional Building Construction received $2.8B and Other Computer Related Services received $2.2B in FY2026 to date."
      }
    ]
  },
